0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 52 651.8898 Tm (2.1 C++ and Programming Paradigms) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 10.1 Tf 12.12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 631.8898 Tm (C++ supports procedural programming through functions and control flow and object-oriented programming through) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 617.8898 Tm (classes and objects. Menu-driven console programs repeatedly display choices, read input and call the relevant operation) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 603.8898 Tm (until the user selects exit.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 12.2 Tf 14.64 TL ET
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 52 581.8898 Tm (2.2 Data Structures for Record Management) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 10.1 Tf 12.12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 561.8898 Tm (Structures or classes group related fields into a logical record. std::vector is suitable for a growing collection of records,) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 547.8898 Tm (std::string manages textual fields and arrays are suitable for fixed-size representations such as a game board.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 12.2 Tf 14.64 TL ET
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 52 525.8898 Tm (2.3 File Handling in C++) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 10.1 Tf 12.12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 505.8898 Tm (The fstream library provides input and output streams for reading and writing files. Persistent storage allows records to) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 491.8898 Tm (remain available after the application closes, provided the program writes valid data and reads it correctly on the next) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 477.8898 Tm (execution.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 12.2 Tf 14.64 TL ET
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 52 455.8898 Tm (2.4 Input Validation and Error Handling) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 10.1 Tf 12.12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 435.8898 Tm (Interactive programs must validate user input before changing data. Typical checks include duplicate identifiers, valid) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 421.8898 Tm (numeric ranges, record existence, sufficient balance and valid state transitions.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 12.2 Tf 14.64 TL ET
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 52 399.8898 Tm (2.5 Tools and Their Purpose) Tj T* ET
BT /F4 10.1 Tf 12.12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 379.8898 Tm (A C++ compiler such as g++ is used to build the programs. A code editor and terminal support writing, compiling and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 52 365.8898 Tm (executing the applications. GitHub can be used to maintain project source and documentation.) Tj T* ET
 

